WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.190
The old way always sounds the same. Tabs open. Notes scattered. A runner sheet half remembered.

2
00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:16.379
The GM buying time while the table waits for the moment to come back alive.

3
00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:24.569
Chummer6 is built for the instant when preparation has to become play.

4
00:00:24.569 --> 00:00:32.758
It gathers the runner, the crew, the scene, the consequence, and the next decision into one surface that can actually survive pressure.

5
00:00:32.758 --> 00:00:40.948
You build with the important details in view: gear, chrome, magic, tradeoffs, and every number explained clearly enough that the table can trust it.

6
00:00:40.948 --> 00:00:49.137
You run with momentum: scenes, handouts, opposition, downtime, hooks, and fallout ready when the room needs them.

7
00:00:49.137 --> 00:00:57.327
And when the city answers, it does not answer as flavor text.

8
00:00:57.327 --> 00:01:05.516
It answers with heat, factions, jobs, and consequences the GM can turn into tomorrow night's trouble.

9
00:01:05.516 --> 00:01:13.706
House rules stop living as arguments in old chat logs. Recaps stop dissolving into rumor. The aftermath becomes signal.

10
00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:21.895
The signal becomes the next run.

11
00:01:21.895 --> 00:01:30.085
From desktop to tablet to phone, from home table to remote night, Chummer6 is for crews who want the world to remember what they did and still be ready when the next door blows open.
